{"id":"mahabharata-3-015","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":15,"title":"पञ्चदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 15 · Krishna tells of Shalva's attack","summary":{"en":"Asked why he was absent, Krishna explains that Shalva, enraged at Shishupala's death, attacked Dvaraka in his flying city Saubha while Krishna was at the Rajasuya. On returning he found the city ravaged and set out to kill Shalva.","kn":"ಏಕೆ ಬರಲಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ, ಶಿಶುಪಾಲನ ಮರಣದಿಂದ ಕೋಪಗೊಂಡ ಶಾಲ್ವನು ತಾನು ರಾಜಸೂಯದಲ್ಲಿದ್ದಾಗ ಹಾರುವ ಸೌಭನಗರದಲ್ಲಿ ದ್ವಾರಕೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ದಾಳಿಮಾಡಿದನು, ಮರಳಿದಾಗ ನಗರ ಧ್ವಂಸವಾಗಿತ್ತು, ಶಾಲ್ವನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲಲು ಹೊರಟೆ ಎಂದು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ವಿವರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अनुपस्थिति का कारण पूछे जाने पर श्रीकृष्ण बताते हैं कि शिशुपाल की मृत्यु से क्रुद्ध शाल्व ने उनके राजसूय में रहते अपने उड़ने वाले नगर सौभ से द्वारका पर आक्रमण किया। लौटने पर उन्होंने नगर को उजड़ा पाया और शाल्व को मारने निकल पड़े।","te":"ఎందుకు రాలేదని అడగగా, శిశుపాలుని మరణంతో కోపించిన శాల్వుడు తాను రాజసూయంలో ఉన్నప్పుడు ఎగిరే సౌభనగరంతో ద్వారకపై దాడి చేశాడని, తిరిగివచ్చేసరికి నగరం ధ్వంసమైందని, శాల్వుని చంపడానికి బయలుదేరానని శ్రీకృష్ణుడు వివరిస్తాడు.","ta":"ஏன் வரவில்லை என்று கேட்க, ஶிஶுபாலனின் மரணத்தால் சினமுற்ற ஶால்வன் தாம் ராஜஸூயத்தில் இருந்தபோது பறக்கும் நகரமான ஸௌபத்தில் வந்து த்வாரகையைத் தாக்கினான், திரும்பியபோது நகரம் சிதைந்திருந்தது, ஶால்வனைக் கொல்லப் புறப்பட்டேன் என்று ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் விளக்குகிறார்.","ml":"എന്തുകൊണ്ട് ഹാജരില്ലായിരുന്നുവെന്ന ചോദ്യത്തിന്, ശിശുപാലന്റെ വധത്തിൽ കുപിതനായ ശാല്വൻ, കൃഷ്ണൻ രാജസൂയത്തിൽ ആയിരിക്കെ, പറക്കുന്ന നഗരമായ സൗഭത്തിൽ ദ്വാരകയെ ആക്രമിച്ചുവെന്ന് കൃഷ്ണൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. മടങ്ങിയെത്തിയപ്പോൾ നഗരം നശിച്ചുകിടക്കുന്നത് കണ്ട് ശാല്വനെ കൊല്ലാൻ അദ്ദേഹം പുറപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.15; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कैरातपर्व","titleEn":"Kairata Parva (The mountain hunter)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"असांनिध्यं कथं कृष्ण तवासीद्वृष्णिनन्दन ।\nक्व चासीद्विप्रवासस्ते किं वाकार्षीः प्रवासकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, joy of the Vrishnis, how were you absent? Where did you stay away, and what did you do while abroad?"}},{"text":"कृष्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"शाल्वस्य नगरं सौभं गतोऽहं भरतर्षभ ।\nविनिहन्तुं नरश्रेष्ठ तत्र मे शृणु कारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bull of the Bharatas, I had gone to Shalva's city Saubha to destroy him. Hear, best of men, my reason."}},{"n":3,"text":"महातेजा महाबाहुर्यः स राजा महायशाः ।\nदमघोषात्मजो वीरः शिशुपालो मया हतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That mighty-armed, glorious king, heroic Shishupala, son of Damaghosha, of great energy, was killed by me."}},{"n":4,"text":"यज्ञे ते भरतश्रेष्ठ राजसूयेऽर्हणां प्रति ।\nस रोषवशसंप्राप्तो नामृष्यत दुरात्मवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At your Rajasuya sacrifice, bull of the Bharatas, over the offering of honor, that wicked man, overcome by rage, could not bear it."}},{"n":5,"text":"श्रुत्वा तं निहतं शाल्वस्तीव्ररोषसमन्वितः ।\nउपायाद्द्वारकां शून्यामिहस्थे मयि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that he was killed, Shalva, filled with fierce anger, came to empty Dvaraka while I was here, descendant of Bharata."}},{"n":6,"text":"स तत्र योधितो राजन्बालकैर्वृष्णिपुंगवैः ।\nआगतः कामगं सौभमारुह्यैव नृशंसकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, king, he was fought by the young Vrishni bulls; the cruel one had come mounted on Saubha, which moves at will."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततो वृष्णिप्रवीरांस्तान्बालान्हत्वा बहूंस्तदा ।\nपुरोद्यानानि सर्वाणि भेदयामास दुर्मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that evil-minded man, having killed many of the young Vrishni heroes, destroyed all the city gardens."}},{"n":8,"text":"उक्तवांश्च महाबाहो क्वासौ वृष्णिकुलाधमः ।\nवासुदेवः सुमन्दात्मा वसुदेवसुतो गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And he said, \"Where is that lowest of the Vrishni line, the dull-minded Vasudeva, son of Vasudeva? Mighty-armed ones, where has he gone?\""}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्य युद्धार्थिनो दर्पं युद्धे नाशयितास्म्यहम् ।\nआनर्ताः सत्यमाख्यात तत्र गन्तास्मि यत्र सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will destroy in battle the pride of one who wants to fight. Anartas, tell me truly: I will go where he is.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"तं हत्वा विनिवर्तिष्ये कंसकेशिनिषूदनम् ।\nअहत्वा न निवर्तिष्ये सत्येनायुधमालभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will return after killing him, the slayer of Kamsa and Keshin; without killing him I will not return. I touch my weapon on this oath.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"क्वासौ क्वासाविति पुनस्तत्र तत्र विधावति ।\nमया किल रणे युद्धं काङ्क्षमाणः स सौभराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again and again he ran here and there, \"Where is he, where?\", that king of Saubha, wishing to fight me in battle."}},{"n":12,"text":"अद्य तं पापकर्माणं क्षुद्रं विश्वासघातिनम् ।\nशिशुपालवधामर्षाद्गमयिष्ये यमक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today, in anger at Shishupala's killing, I will send that sinful, petty traitor to Yama's abode.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"मम पापस्वभावेन भ्राता येन निपातितः ।\nशिशुपालो महीपालस्तं वधिष्ये महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will kill on the ground that Shishupala, king of the earth, my brother, who was struck down by his sinful nature.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"भ्राता बालश्च राजा च न च संग्राममूर्धनि ।\nप्रमत्तश्च हतो वीरस्तं हनिष्ये जनार्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brother, a boy and a king, was killed not at the head of a battle but while unwary; I will kill that Janardana.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"एवमादि महाराज विलप्य दिवमास्थितः ।\nकामगेन स सौभेन क्षिप्त्वा मां कुरुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lamenting thus and more, great king, he rose into the sky, and, having struck at me, joy of the Kurus, went off on his Saubha that goes where it wills."}},{"n":16,"text":"तमश्रौषमहं गत्वा यथा वृत्तः सुदुर्मतिः ।\nमयि कौरव्य दुष्टात्मा मार्त्तिकावतको नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I went and heard how that very evil-minded king of Martikavata had acted against me, descendant of Kuru."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततोऽहमपि कौरव्य रोषव्याकुललोचनः ।\nनिश्चित्य मनसा राजन्वधायास्य मनो दधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I too, Kauravya, with eyes agitated by anger, made up my mind and set my heart on killing him."}},{"n":18,"text":"आनर्तेषु विमर्दं च क्षेपं चात्मनि कौरव ।\nप्रवृद्धमवलेपं च तस्य दुष्कृतकर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I considered the havoc among the Anartas, the insult to me, and the growing arrogance of that evil-doer."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततः सौभवधायाहं प्रतस्थे पृथिवीपते ।\nस मया सागरावर्ते दृष्ट आसीत्परीप्सता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, lord of earth, I set out to destroy Saubha. I saw him in the whirlpool of the sea, as I sought him."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः प्रध्माप्य जलजं पाञ्चजन्यमहं नृप ।\nआहूय शाल्वं समरे युद्धाय समवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, blowing my conch Panchajanya, I challenged Shalva and stood ready for battle."}},{"n":21,"text":"सुमुहूर्तमभूद्युद्धं तत्र मे दानवैः सह ।\nवशीभूताश्च मे सर्वे भूतले च निपातिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A very good while the fight went on there between me and the Danavas, and all of them were brought under my power and felled to the ground."}},{"n":22,"text":"एतत्कार्यं महाबाहो येनाहं नागमं तदा ।\nश्रुत्वैव हास्तिनपुरं द्यूतं चाविनयोत्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This was the matter, mighty-armed one, for which I did not come then, since I heard of Hastinapura and the dice game arisen from a lack of restraint."}}]}]}